cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference OCOM, please cite it as below."
title: "OCOM: the Object-Centric Operating Model"
abstract: >-
  An open, technology-independent specification that describes an organization
  as a system of governed objects with identity, ownership, lifecycle, and
  evidence, where dashboards, documents, graphs, indexes and agent context are
  rebuildable projections of that governed source rather than second sources of
  truth.
